    "https://millsaps.edu/job-listings/data-and-information-systems-specialist-institutional-advancement/": {
      "title": "Data and Information Systems Specialist (Institutional Advancement)",
      "description": "Data and Information Systems Specialist (Institutional Advancement) - Millsaps College Skip to main content Contact Millsaps Visit Apply Give Millsaps homepage Millsaps homepage MENU Apply Visit Give Info for Prospective Students Current Students Transfer Students Alumni Faculty & Staff Family & Community Contact Millsaps Apply Visit Give About About Millsaps Get to Know Us Why Millsaps News Events College Leadership Giving Directory Major Resources FAQs Admissions & Aid Admissions & Aid Visit Millsaps Apply to Millsaps Secure Your Spot Financial Aid & Scholarships Cost & Value Admitted Students Transfer Students International Students Info For Family & Community Follow Us On Social Academics Academics Overview The Millsaps Experience Find Your Program Areas of Study Departments Majors & Minors Academic Resources More Ways to Learn Student Success Services Study Abroad Major Resources Millsaps-Wilson Library Course Connect College Catalog Campus Campus Life Chaplain & Church Relations New Students Start Here Traditions Living on Campus Eating on Campus Get Involved Fitness & Health Athletics Give Give Give Now Ways to Give Planned Giving Annual Fund Else School of Management Graduate School Executive Education © 2025 Millsaps College. All right reserved Privacy Policy Title IX Follow Follow Follow Follow Start of main content. Data and Information Systems Specialist (Institutional Advancement) Job Summary The Data and Information Systems Specialist reports to the Director of Advancement Information Systems and is responsible for data collection, entry, management, analysis and reporting of information to support fundraising, alumni and parent relations, and donor stewardship efforts. As part of the Advancement Services team, the responsibilities of this job are central to the effectiveness of fund raising and alumni engagement efforts at Millsaps College. This is a full-time position that works on-site in Jackson, MS with regular office hours from 8:00am – 4:30pm with a one-hour unpaid lunch break. Evening and weekend work is occasionally required to support major events and initiatives. Job Duties Data Specialist Accurately record and enter data into database and/or other management systems either through manual or electronic processes. Execute data acquisition projects. Monitor and maintain data integrity to ensure accuracy, completeness, and consistency of information. Conduct periodic audits and validation checks to identify and rectify gaps and discrepancies in data. Train and oversee student employees to assist with data entry projects, ensuring accuracy and timely delivery of updated information. Ensure compliance with relevant data protection and privacy regulations. Generate reports and assist with data transfers between digital platforms. Gift Processing and Stewardship Process a minimum of $10 million in gifts, securities, in-kind gifts, deferred gifts and pledges annually Daily process gifts and pledges including those made by check, via online and other credit cards, electronic fund transfer, payroll deduction, etc. Ensure proper gift/pledge documentation is provided, scanned and digitally filed Collaborate with Advancement Staff and Business Office to develop fund accounts as needed Maintain accuracy of giving records for all donors Produce and distribute all gift receipts within 48 hours of gift being received Facilitate gift acknowledgment template process through Communications Module Produce daily gift reports and submit gifts to the Business Office for deposit. Work with the Business Office to resolve any discrepancies or data errors as quickly as possible Interact with donors as needed and assist them with questions regarding their gifts and / or pledges Produce and distribute regular pledge reminders in cooperation with fundraising staff Administer matching gift program including tracking, submitting, and filing forms Produce regular and ad hoc gift reports including but not limited to: Daily gift reports to Advancement staff Monthly gift reports to Advancement staff and designation reports to college departments Account reconciliations as needed Campaign updates as needed Maintain up-to-date knowledge of CASE (Council for Advancement and Support of Education) Management Reporting Standards, IRS substantiation regulations and FASB (Financial Accounting Standard Board) standards. Work closely with Advancement Staff to maintain proper procedures and ensure Millsaps is in compliance with standards. Develop and maintain gift processing operations and standards manual. Qualifications Bachelor’s degree in a relevant field or an equivalent mix of education and experience One to two years’ experience working with data entry, auditing, analysis , and reporting Experience in or familiarity with fundraising, accounting, banking, finance and/or customer service if preferred Ability to learn new systems quickly Strong working knowledge of Microsoft Office, particularly Word and Excel Excellent written, oral, and interpersonal communication skills. Strong curiosity, problem solving, organizational and time management skills with ability to handle concurrent tasks which are time sensitive Proven accuracy and attention to detail Proven ability to exercise initiative and sound judgment Highly ethical with ability to maintain confidential information Ability to work independently and as part of a collaborative team Physical & Availability Requirements Must be able to work on campus daily to receive and process gifts Prolonged periods sitting at a desk and working on a computer Manual dexterity needed for keyboarding and other repetitive tasks Must be able to lift and move up to 25 pounds without assistance Application Procedure Applicants should submit a current resume, and a letter of interest [email protected] . Please write “Data and Information Systems Specialist” in the subject line of the email. View More Job Opportunities About Millsaps Millsaps College is a selective institution of higher education located on 100 beautiful acres in the heart of Jackson, the capital of Mississippi — a progressive southern metropolitan city of nearly half a million. Millsaps is dedicated to academic excellence, open inquiry and free expression, the exploration of faith to inform vocation and the innovative shaping of the social, economic and cultural progress of the region. The college was founded in 1890 by members of the Methodist Church and is consistently ranked as one of the best values in higher education. Millsaps has an enrollment of approximately 750 students and employs 80 full-time faculty members. The faculty/student ratio at Millsaps is 1:9, and the average class size is 14. Millsaps has graduated 25 Fulbright Award recipients, seven Rhodes Scholars, six Goldwater Scholars and two Truman Scholars. Millsaps is a member of the NCAA Division III and Southern Athletic Association and competes in 18 intercollegiate sports. EEO Statement Millsaps College values diversity within our students, faculty and staff, and strives to recruit, develop, and retain the most talented people. Millsaps College does not discriminate in employment on the bases of race, color, creed, religion, sex, sexual orientation, transgender status, gender identity, age, national origin, disability, veteran status or any other legally protected status in accordance with applicable federal, state and/or local laws. All offers of employment will be contingent on successful completion of a background check and verification of employment. Salary will be commensurate with experience. Millsaps College provides a competitive benefits package . It is the policy of Millsaps College to provide reasonable accommodations for qualified individuals with disabilities for employment. If you require any accommodations to participate in any part of the hiring process, please contact [email protected] . Additional Information In compliance with the amendments to the federal Clery Act concerning annual security reports, all potential job applicants are free to view Millsaps College’s annual Campus Crime Statistics here . The only national liberal arts college in Mississippi, Millsaps College has consistently been ranked a “Best Buy” among national liberal arts colleges by U.S. News and World Report ‘s America’s Best Colleges and is cited as one of Loren Pope’s 40 Colleges That Change Lives . It was the first institution in Mississippi with a Phi Beta Kappa chapter, and is the only institution in Mississippi ever to be listed in The Fiske Guide to Colleges . Millsaps is a member of the ACS and NITLE , and has an AACSB accredited business school. In accordance with Federal law, we are making available our Campus Security Report to all prospective employees. Millsaps is located in Jackson, the capital of the state. The Jackson area has a population of around 400,000 and offers low cost-of-living, excellent schools, pleasant climate, and many recreational opportunities. For additional information about Millsaps College please visit the links below: Academic Programs Athletics Title IX compliance Employee Benefits Accessibility Accreditation Apply Now Bookstore Campus Map Campus Safety Contact Us COVID-19 Info Else School of Management Job Opportunities Library Privacy/Legal Notice Request Info Student Achievement Student Consumer Information and Disclosures Title IX Apply Visit Give Follow Follow Follow Follow NONDISCRIMINATION POLICY Millsaps College admits students of any race, color, national and ethnic origin to all the rights, privileges, programs, and activities generally accorded or made available to students at the school. It does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national and ethnic origin in administration of its educational policies, admissions policies, scholarship and loan programs, and athletic and other school-administered programs. © Copyright 2025 Millsaps College. All rights reserved. A United Methodist–Related College. Manage your privacy To provide the best experience, we use cookies to store and/or access device information. Consenting will allow us to process this data. Functional Functional Always active The technical storage or access is strictly necessary for the legitimate purpose of enabling the use of a specific service explicitly requested by the subscriber or user, or for the sole purpose of carrying out the transmission of a communication over an electronic communications network. Preferences Preferences The technical storage or access is necessary for the legitimate purpose of storing preferences that are not requested by the subscriber or user. Statistics Statistics The technical storage or access that is used exclusively for statistical purposes. The technical storage or access that is used exclusively for anonymous statistical purposes. Without a subpoena, voluntary compliance on the part of your Internet Service Provider, or additional records from a third party, information stored or retrieved for this purpose alone cannot usually be used to identify you. Marketing Marketing The technical storage or access is required to create user profiles to send advertising, or to track the user on a website or across several websites for similar marketing purposes. Manage options Manage services Manage {vendor_count} vendors Read more about these purposes Accept Deny Manage options Save preferences Manage options {title} {title} {title} Manage consent"
