    "https://millsaps.edu/work-at-millsaps/": {
      "title": "Work",
      "description": "Work at Millsaps - Join Our Passionate Team Skip to main content Contact Millsaps Visit Apply Give Millsaps homepage Millsaps homepage MENU Apply Visit Give Info for Prospective Students Current Students Transfer Students Alumni Faculty & Staff Family & Community Contact Millsaps Apply Visit Give About About Millsaps Get to Know Us Why Millsaps News Events College Leadership Giving Directory Major Resources FAQs Admissions & Aid Admissions & Aid Visit Millsaps Apply to Millsaps Secure Your Spot Financial Aid & Scholarships Cost & Value Admitted Students Transfer Students International Students Info For Family & Community Follow Us On Social Academics Academics Overview The Millsaps Experience Find Your Program Areas of Study Departments Majors & Minors Academic Resources More Ways to Learn Student Success Services Study Abroad Major Resources Millsaps-Wilson Library Course Connect College Catalog Campus Campus Life Chaplain & Church Relations New Students Start Here Traditions Living on Campus Eating on Campus Get Involved Fitness & Health Athletics Give Give Give Now Ways to Give Planned Giving Annual Fund Else School of Management Graduate School Executive Education © 2025 Millsaps College. All right reserved Privacy Policy Title IX Follow Follow Follow Follow Start of main content. Work at Millsaps Major career opportunities Millsaps is dedicated to academic excellence, open inquiry and free expression, the exploration of faith to inform vocation and the innovative shaping of the social, economic and cultural progress of the region. Our faculty and staff are invested in helping our students Become Something Major. Join us! Open Positions Faculty Careers Explore current academic job openings at Millsaps for opportunities to contribute to a vibrant intellectual community focused on academic excellence. Staff Careers Discover how you can make an impact at Millsaps College. You will find rewarding opportunities where you can make MAJOR contributions. Assistant Tennis Coach Assistant Women’s Soccer Coach Associate Vice President of Institutional Advancement Campus Safety Officer (part-time) Data and Information Systems Specialist (Institutional Advancement) Director of Development Registrar Student Jobs Are you a student wanting to find on-campus work? Maybe land an internship to jumpstart your career? Check out the ways you can seek student employment. On-campus employment is often an early way students engage with the world of work. As supervisors of student-employees, faculty and staff provide important career and professional development experiences for students and can contribute richly to a student’s long-term career success. To view open positions, students should log in to Major Careers. About Us Millsaps College is a selective institution of higher education located on 100 beautiful acres in the heart of Jackson, the capital of Mississippi — a progressive Southern metropolitan city of nearly half a million. The college was founded in 1890 by members of the Methodist Church and is consistently ranked as one of the best values in higher education. The faculty/student ratio at Millsaps is 1:9, and the average class size is 14. Millsaps has graduated 28 Fulbright Award recipients, seven Rhodes Scholars, six Goldwater Scholars and two Truman Scholars. Millsaps is a member of the NCAA Division III and Southern Athletic Association and competes in 18 intercollegiate sports. Equal Employment Opportunity Millsaps College values diversity within our community, students, faculty and staff, and strives to recruit, develop and retain the most talented people. Millsaps College does not discriminate in employment on the basis of race, color, creed, religion, sex, sexual orientation, transgender status, gender identity, age, national origin, disability, veteran status or any other legally protected status in accordance with applicable federal, state and/or local laws. All offers of employment will be contingent on successful completion of a background check and verification of employment. Salary will be commensurate with experience. Millsaps College provides a competitive benefits package. It is the policy of Millsaps College to provide reasonable accommodations for qualified individuals with disabilities. If you require any accommodations to participate in any part of the hiring process, please contact [email protected] . Required notices In compliance with the amendments to the federal Clery Act concerning annual security reports, all potential job applicants are free to view Millsaps College’s annual Campus Crime Statistics here . The only national liberal arts college in Mississippi, Millsaps College has consistently been ranked a “Best Buy” among national liberal arts colleges by U.S. News and World Report‘s America’s Best Colleges and is cited as one of Loren Pope’s 40 Colleges That Change Lives. It was the first institution in Mississippi with a Phi Beta Kappa chapter and is the only institution in Mississippi ever to be listed in The Fiske Guide to Colleges. Millsaps is a member of the ACS and NITLE, has an AACSB accredited business school and an NCATE accredited education program. In accordance with federal law, we are making available our Campus Security Report to all prospective employees. Millsaps is located in Jackson, the capital of the state. The Jackson area has a population of around 400,000 and offers a low cost of living, excellent schools, pleasant climate and many recreational opportunities. For additional information about Millsaps College, please visit the links below: Academic Programs Athletics Title IX Compliance Employee Benefits Benefits Overview Comprehensive health and wellness benefits including medical, dental and vision benefits Flexible spending accounts for health and dependent care expenses 403B retirement plan with Millsaps contributions Paid holidays, vacation and sick time Tuition remission benefits for staff, administrators and faculty Additional perks and discounts Learn more about our community, check out our benefits information or apply today for one of our open positions. Accessibility Accreditation Apply Now Bookstore Campus Map Campus Safety Contact Us COVID-19 Info Else School of Management Job Opportunities Library Privacy/Legal Notice Request Info Student Achievement Student Consumer Information and Disclosures Title IX Apply Visit Give Follow Follow Follow Follow NONDISCRIMINATION POLICY Millsaps College admits students of any race, color, national and ethnic origin to all the rights, privileges, programs, and activities generally accorded or made available to students at the school. It does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national and ethnic origin in administration of its educational policies, admissions policies, scholarship and loan programs, and athletic and other school-administered programs. © Copyright 2025 Millsaps College. All rights reserved. A United Methodist–Related College. Manage your privacy To provide the best experience, we use cookies to store and/or access device information. Consenting will allow us to process this data. Functional Functional Always active The technical storage or access is strictly necessary for the legitimate purpose of enabling the use of a specific service explicitly requested by the subscriber or user, or for the sole purpose of carrying out the transmission of a communication over an electronic communications network. Preferences Preferences The technical storage or access is necessary for the legitimate purpose of storing preferences that are not requested by the subscriber or user. Statistics Statistics The technical storage or access that is used exclusively for statistical purposes. The technical storage or access that is used exclusively for anonymous statistical purposes. Without a subpoena, voluntary compliance on the part of your Internet Service Provider, or additional records from a third party, information stored or retrieved for this purpose alone cannot usually be used to identify you. Marketing Marketing The technical storage or access is required to create user profiles to send advertising, or to track the user on a website or across several websites for similar marketing purposes. Manage options Manage services Manage {vendor_count} vendors Read more about these purposes Accept Deny Manage options Save preferences Manage options {title} {title} {title} Manage consent"
